<title>USA: Federal-Mogul vice president resigns.</title>
<headline>Federal-Mogul vice president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich. 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal-Mogul Corp said Monday Harold Parkison resigned as vice president - international store development effective January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Parkison will become president and chief executive officer of Forest City Auto Parts, a wholly owned subsidiary of Tyler Corp. Forest City Auto is a customer of Federal-Mogul.</p>
<p>Federal-Mogul makes and distributes parts for automobiles, trucks and farm and construction vehicles.</p>
<p>	   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
